==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|défaitisme}}, coined in 1915 by Russian writer {{w|Grigory Aleksinsky|Grigorij Aleksinskij}} as a translation of {{cog|ru|пораже́нчество}}, also coined by him as a derivation of {{m|ru|порази́ть||to strike, defeat}}. {{surf|en|defeat|-ism}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/dɪˈfiːtɪzəm/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-defeatism.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# [[acceptance|Acceptance]] of defeat [[without]] [[struggle]].
#: ''Objective assessment is good, but '''defeatism''' will reduce our potentials even when the prospects for victory have never been nearer.''

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|defeatist}}

